    {"op": "advance_seconds", "seconds": 0.5},
    {"op": "note", "text": "How a TTW new game reaches Vault 101 [observed]: TaleOfTwoWastelands.esm gives no quest the start-game flag for its opening; New Game starts the quest the INI's sCharGenQuest names, and TTW's INI line is SCharGenQuest=001FFFF8, the quest TTWStart (engine/nvf-play game_start.rs notes). The headless runner does not start it, so the chain gives TTWStart running and a menu open (the new game's loading screen, 1007) so its MenuMode block runs: the player is put at TTWHoldingCellPlayerXMarkerREF, the country radio is disabled and the four VPreorder quests stop. When the menu closes its GameMode shows TTWStartMessage: button 0 (Start in Capital Wasteland) sets the global bInDCWasteland and CG00 stage 0, the Fallout 3 birth scene; button 1 (Start in Mojave Wasteland) gives CG04DadNote, starts MQ01 and plays New Vegas's VCG00 opening instead. VCG01 is start-game enabled in TTW as in New Vegas and waits for VCG00, so it stays at stage 0 on the Capital start."},
    {"op": "note", "text": "This chain plays the Capital Wasteland start: CG00 (birth) leads into CG01 Baby Steps, CG02 Growing Up Fast, CG03 Future Imperfect and CG04 Escape!, which only make sense in sequence (each one's last stage starts the next); CG04's last stage sets MQ01 10."},
